abstract: >
  SEME (Signed concordance, Effect-vector fidelity, Magnitude transfer,
  Encoding retention) is an evaluation protocol for literature-constrained,
  chemistry-conditioned EEG generative models, demonstrated on a
  pharmacodynamically penalized Donepezil/Memantine CVAE case study.
keywords:
  - SEME
  - EEG
  - CVAE
  - evaluation protocol
  - pharmacodynamic constraints
